  {
    "title": "File:A NASA drone photo offers a bird’s-eye view of the B-2 Test Stand at NASA’s Stennis Space Center with the first flight core stage for NASA’s new Space Launch System (SLS) (2020-02-09 - Artemis I Core Stage on the B-2 Stand - 02).jpg",
    "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/A_NASA_drone_photo_offers_a_bird%E2%80%99s-eye_view_of_the_B-2_Test_Stand_at_NASA%E2%80%99s_Stennis_Space_Center_with_the_first_flight_core_stage_for_NASA%E2%80%99s_new_Space_Launch_System_%28SLS%29_%282020-02-09_-_Artemis_I_Core_Stage_on_the_B-2_Stand_-_02%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_NASA_drone_photo_offers_a_bird%E2%80%99s-eye_view_of_the_B-2_Test_Stand_at_NASA%E2%80%99s_Stennis_Space_Center_with_the_first_flight_core_stage_for_NASA%E2%80%99s_new_Space_Launch_System_(SLS)_(2020-02-09_-_Artemis_I_Core_Stage_on_the_B-2_Stand_-_02).jpg",
    "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/A_NASA_drone_photo_offers_a_bird%E2%80%99s-eye_view_of_the_B-2_Test_Stand_at_NASA%E2%80%99s_Stennis_Space_Center_with_the_first_flight_core_stage_for_NASA%E2%80%99s_new_Space_Launch_System_%28SLS%29_%282020-02-09_-_Artemis_I_Core_Stage_on_the_B-2_Stand_-_02%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
    "license": "Public domain",
    "artist": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/stennis/\">NASA Stennis Space Center</a>",
    "description": "A NASA drone photo offers a bird’s-eye view of the B-2 Test Stand at NASA’s Stennis Space Center with the first flight core stage for NASA’s new Space Launch System (SLS) installed for Green Run testing. The SLS core stage is undergoing a series of tests on its integrated systems prior to its use on the Artemis I mission. NASA is building SLS to return humans, including the first woman, to the Moon as part of the Artemis program and to prepare for eventual missions to Mars. The Green Run series at Stennis culminates with a hot fire of the core stage’s four RS-25 engines, just as during an actual launch."
  },
  {
    "title": "File:Bird-drone interaction.webm",
    "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Bird-drone_interaction.webm/1280px--Bird-drone_interaction.webm.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo",
    "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bird-drone_interaction.webm",
    "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/67/Bird-drone_interaction.webm?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
    "license": "CC BY 3.0",
    "artist": "Scott Elkins",
    "description": "Bird–drone interaction. Filmed on Eagle Mountain Lake, Texas, USA. Interaction means \"affecting each other\", but in this video title it is a rather loosely applied term meaning that the drone reacts to and follows the birds' movements not by itself but via the drone operator. The birds can be thought to be fleeing the drone because it resembles a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird_of_prey\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Bird of prey\">raptor</a>.\nIn this video, the original material has been muted and trimmed."
  },
